cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Himalayan expedition success: predicting whether an expedition reaches the summit with a logistic regression"
abstract: >-
  Data processing project on the Himalayan Expeditions dataset (Kaggle, from
  The Himalayan Database): exploration and wrangling with pandas, selection of
  the predictors known before departure to avoid data leakage, handcrafted
  features tested against the data, and a logistic regression in a
  scikit-learn pipeline validated by cross-validation. The model reaches 69.3 %
  of accuracy against a 55 % baseline, with supplemental oxygen, the commercial
  route and the difficulty of the peak as the main factors.
